    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "`nvim_call_dict_function()` calls `abort()` instead of returning or raising an error when its dict expression fails to evaluate while errors are suppressed with `:silent!`.\n\n```vim\nsilent! call nvim_call_dict_function(\"g:Missing\", \"strlen\", [])\n```\n\n```\nnvim --headless -u NONE -i NONE -n -c 'silent! call nvim_call_dict_function(\"g:Missing\", \"strlen\", [])' -c 'echo \"alive\"' -c q\n```\n\nWith an ASan build:\n\n```\n==654==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: ABRT on unknown address 0x1442950000028e (pc 0x7f4d903d19bc bp 0x00000000028e sp 0x7ffd17d96b60 T0)\n    #2 0x7f4d903637f2 in abort (/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6+0x287f2)\n    #3 0x555eca29cdeb in nvim_call_dict_function src/nvim/api/vimscript.c:300\n    #4 0x555eca344a81 in handle_nvim_call_dict_function build/src/nvim/auto/api/private/dispatch_wrappers.generated.h:10799\n    #5 0x555eca57ce26 in api_wrapper src/nvim/eval/funcs.c:376\n    #6 0x555eca592183 in call_internal_func src/nvim/eval/funcs.c:292\nSUMMARY: AddressSanitizer: ABRT (/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6+0x969bc) in pthread_kill\n```\n\nExpected: the call fails like it does without `silent!`, where it gives `E5555: API call: Vim:E121: Undefined variable: g:Missing`; with `:silent!` it should just return without aborting, and \"alive\" should be echoed.\n\nFound at a054b698c0b7c83e934a38df5c0021ae2cb444cc; it still reproduces at 9b7ec59580fd. The ASan build exits with rc 1 and the report above. The release build exits with rc 134 (SIGABRT) and prints nothing.\n\nLooks like `nvim_call_dict_function` in `src/nvim/api/vimscript.c` assumes that `eval0()` returning FAIL always means an API error was set; with `emsg_silent` the error is suppressed, so it reaches `abort();  // Should not happen.`.\n\nI can send a patch if that helps.\n\nFound with an LLM-based testing tool; I used Claude to reduce it and look for the cause.\n",
